# name: test/client/sql/cluster_trust_unrelated_ca.test
# description: live: on the provisioned cluster, with SSL_CERT_FILE naming a CA that signs no endpoint, the connect fails as a certificate failure
# group: [sql]

# Live only, in a process whose SSL_CERT_FILE names a CA that signed none of the endpoints, with
# REDSHIFT_TEST_LIVE_UNRELATED_CA_REGION naming the live region (test/README.md, "Live variables").
require-env REDSHIFT_TEST_CLIENT odbc

require-env REDSHIFT_TEST_LIVE_UNRELATED_CA_REGION

require-env REDSHIFT_TEST_LIVE_CLUSTER

# On Windows the control plane verifies against the Windows store whatever SSL_CERT_FILE says, as in
# trust_unrelated_ca.test, so this case does not run on Windows.
require notwindows

require redshift

# The connect fails with a certificate error, which the certificate rule reads. The runner adds a
# newline before it full-matches.
statement error
ATTACH '' AS rs (TYPE redshift, REGION '{REDSHIFT_TEST_LIVE_UNRELATED_CA_REGION}', CREDENTIAL_PROVIDER aws_default_chain, CLUSTER '{REDSHIFT_TEST_LIVE_CLUSTER}');
----
<REGEX>:(?s)IO Error: Cannot attach rs: Could not connect to Redshift at [^\n]*: the server's TLS certificate could not be verified\.\nCheck the trusted CA certificates, from SSL_CERT_FILE or the system store, and the network path to the Redshift host\. Verification cannot be turned off\.\nSQLSTATE: HY000\n.*
